What is Recursion?

Recursion means a method calling itself.

Basic example
class Main {
    static void fun(int n) {
        if (n == 0)
            return;

        System.out.println(n);
        fun(n - 1);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        fun(5);
    }
}


Two Important Parts

Every recursion program mainly has 2 parts.

① Base Case

Stops the recursion.

if (n == 0)
    return;
② Recursive Call

Method calls itself.

fun(n - 1);
Easy memory
Base Case       → STOP
Recursive Call  → CONTINUE



