Factorial

Formula:

5! = 5 × 4 × 3 × 2 × 1

Recursive formula:

fact(n) = n × fact(n-1)
Java
class Main {
    static int fact(int n) {
        if (n == 0)
            return 1;

        return n * fact(n - 1);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println(fact(5));
    }
}


Sum of N Numbers

Find:

1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + 5 = 15
class Main {
    static int sum(int n) {
        if (n == 0)
            return 0;

        return n + sum(n - 1);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println(sum(5));
    }
}


Power of a Number

Find:

2³ = 8
class Main {
    static int power(int a, int n) {
        if (n == 0)
            return 1;

        return a * power(a, n - 1);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println(power(2, 3));
    }
}


Sum of Digits

Example:

1234 → 1 + 2 + 3 + 4 = 10
class Main {
    static int sum(int n) {
        if (n == 0)
            return 0;

        return n % 10 + sum(n / 10);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println(sum(1234));
    }
}
